Every catalogue is keyed on a callee name and the analyzer emitted a `calls`
edge only for a function APPLICATION. A zero-argument IO action is a bare
identifier in every position it appears, so `s <- getLine` produced nothing
while `s <- readProcess "uname" [] ""` in the identical flow shape produced an
edge. The row's boundary was irrelevant -- INV-muvis had already moved
Prelude's rows to ipc_recv and the calls stayed just as undetectable. Fixing a
row does not make it reachable.

Emits for the three positions where a bare identifier is unambiguously
EXECUTED: the right-hand side of a `<-` bind, a bare `do` statement, and the
argument of a combinator whose only purpose is to run an action. Fails closed
on a name the enclosing definition binds for itself, matching the rule
_hs_classify_handle_text already states in this module.

The infix operators are excluded on MEASUREMENT, not oversight. Haskell spells
fmap over Maybe, lists and Either with the same operators it spells IO with,
and without types the two are indistinguishable. Over eight repositories they
would add 63 catalogued sites for 3,812 more at 18-35% naming a local binding,
against the 442 of 505 (87.5%) the three covered positions reach at the three
lowest wrong-edge rates. A test pins the trade so a later reader must
re-measure rather than assume.

A/B, both arms cold in their own XDG_CACHE_HOME with the baseline asserted by
grepping the runtime file: 1,916 -> 2,239 I/O chains, +323, ZERO lost, all
haskell. Three read back against source (simplex-chat Bot.hs:35 `void getLine`,
stack FileWatch.hs:108, yesod AddHandler.hs:73).

The population is 505 sites, not the 19 the item scoped to: the same mechanism
hid every zero-argument row in the catalogue, and getCurrentTime (220),
getCurrentDirectory (20), getArgs (17), getEnvironment (17) and exitFailure
(16) dominate the four Prelude stdin readers the item named.

CORRECTS THE ITEM'S FILED POPULATION. simplex-chat is a symlink into
cohort6_crypto/simplex-chat/ and all 267 of cohort6_crypto's .hs files live
under it, so the two paths are one repository. The item's per-repo tally reads
"cohort6_crypto 6, simplex-chat 6" for one set of six: its 25 sites over 9
repositories is 19 over 8. A first pass of this measurement made the same
mistake and reported 794 catalogued sites where there are 505.

test_a_reader_with_no_arguments_is_not_stamped is RE-POINTED, not deleted: it
